  ('apologizing-well', 208, 'Notice whether you apologize to your boss more readily than to people you manage, and even it out once today.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 209, 'Tell someone in customer service that you know the problem isn''t their fault before explaining your issue.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 210, 'Offer to cover a shift or task for a coworker you inconvenienced, as a concrete repair.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 211, 'Admit a misjudgment to a friend who you told off based on a rumor, and say where you went wrong.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 212, 'Write a two-line apology for a meeting you ran over time, and end the next one five minutes early.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 213, 'When a stranger apologizes for bumping you, say "No harm done" warmly and mean it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 214, 'Tell your carpool you''re sorry for making everyone late, and be ready ten minutes early next time.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 215, 'Apologize to a library or shop for a late or damaged item, and pay the fee cheerfully.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 216, 'Send a brief follow-up to a coworker a week after your apology, asking if the new process is working.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 217, 'Review a work email thread where things went wrong and write one line naming your part, even if others had more.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 218, 'Tell a neighbor you''re sorry the leaves or snow from your yard ended up on theirs, and help clear it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 219, 'Wave or nod at a driver you cut off, owning it in the moment, and give extra space for the rest of the drive.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 220, 'Write a long apology you owe, then cut it in half, then cut it in half again, and see what''s left.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 221, 'Notice when "I was tired" or "I was stressed" slips into your apology, and save the context for later if they ask.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 222, 'Say an apology today and then count silently to five before adding anything else.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 223, 'Look for one situation today where someone else''s feelings are theirs to manage, and choose not to apologize for them.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 224, 'Write "I am allowed to make mistakes and fix them" on a card and keep it where you work.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 225, 'Picture a friend making your latest mistake, and write what you''d say to them, then read it to yourself.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 226, 'Decline a request today with "No, thank you" or "That won''t work for me," leaving out the "sorry."'),
  ('apologizing-well', 227, 'Ask yourself before an apology: did I cause harm, or am I just uncomfortable? Let the answer guide what you say.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 228, 'Notice when you apologize for your feelings, like crying or being excited, and try "I feel strongly about this" instead.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 229, 'After a mistake, put your hand on your chest, breathe slowly three times, and say "This is a normal human moment."'),
  ('apologizing-well', 230, 'Write down the mistake you''re most embarrassed about from this year, then list three things you did right that same week.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 231, 'Skip apologizing for your home being messy when a guest arrives, and just welcome them in.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 232, 'Resist apologizing for asking a necessary question at a doctor''s office or the bank, and simply ask it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 233, 'Take a walk in the evening air and let a mistake from today stay behind on the path.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 234, 'Say "I needed a little more time" instead of "Sorry I''m so slow" the next time you take a moment to think.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 235, 'Stop explaining your reasons after the first one in any apology today, and see if anyone asks for more.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 236, 'Notice where you apologize for having a need, such as a quiet workspace, and state the need plainly.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 237, 'Write your inner critic''s harshest line about a mistake, then rewrite it as a fair coworker would say it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 238, 'Keep your apology about the other person''s experience, and leave your own guilt out of the spotlight.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 239, 'Refuse to apologize for someone else''s behavior, like a relative''s rudeness, and let them own it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 240, 'Think of an apology you made that was really a request for reassurance, and notice how it felt afterward.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 241, 'Put a small stone or token in your pocket as a reminder that one mistake doesn''t define your whole day.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 242, 'Say "I disagree" in a conversation today without softening it with "sorry, but."'),
  ('apologizing-well', 243, 'Journal about one mistake you have fully repaired, and give yourself permission to stop replaying it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 244, 'When someone apologizes to you and you are not ready to forgive, say "Thank you, I need some time."'),
  ('apologizing-well', 245, 'Let someone apologize to you without cutting them off or saying "don''t worry about it" too quickly.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 246, 'Notice when you want to pile on self-criticism during an apology, and keep the focus on repair.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 247, 'Do something restful after owning a big mistake, like a bath, a nap or a slow cup of tea, without earning it first.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 248, 'Write down a boundary you held recently that someone disliked, and remind yourself it needed no apology.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 249, 'Tell someone "I''d rather not share the details" if you catch yourself over-explaining a personal choice.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 250, 'Hear an apology from a coworker today and respond with "I appreciate you saying that," then move on to the work.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 251, 'List what''s in your control about a recent mistake, and what isn''t, on two sides of a page.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 252, 'Ask yourself whether you''re apologizing for being yourself, like your laugh or your accent, and let that go.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 253, 'Forgive yourself for a late apology you are still making, because late can still be meaningful.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 254, 'Notice if you apologize to your own body, like "sorry, I''m so out of shape," and swap in something kind.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 255, 'When someone thanks you, say "You''re welcome" instead of "Sorry it took so long."'),
  ('apologizing-well', 256, 'Stop apologizing for the weather, traffic, or other things you can''t control when hosting a guest.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 257, 'Write a note to your future self about how you want to handle your next mistake, and date it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 258, 'When you say sorry to yourself for a mistake, add one concrete next step, like "I''ll set two alarms."'),
  ('apologizing-well', 259, 'Reread a past apology you received and consider whether you ever let the other person know you''d forgiven them.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 260, 'Ask yourself if you''re holding onto an old apology you received that you never accepted, and decide what to do with it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 261, 'Keep an apology you owe short enough to fit in a single text message, even if you''ll say it in person.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 262, 'Notice how often you say "sorry, quick question" at work, and try "I have a quick question" for the rest of the day.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 263, 'Say "I made a mistake" to yourself in the mirror in a neutral voice, as if reading the weather.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 264, 'Practice letting silence sit for a few seconds after someone accepts your apology, without filling it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 265, 'Don''t apologize for taking a lunch break today, and take the full time you''re given.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 266, 'When you realize you were right in a disagreement, resist gloating, and thank the other person for hearing you out.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 267, 'Write one sentence acknowledging a mistake that was partly yours, and leave out the part that belongs to others.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 268, 'Remind yourself that an apology can be sincere and brief at the same time, then write one that proves it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 269, 'Take your apology off the table if it has turned into a plea, and simply ask what the other person needs.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 270, 'Notice a moment when someone over-apologizes to you, and tell them warmly that it''s fine and they did nothing wrong.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 271, 'Choose to not apologize when you speak up for a friend who was treated unfairly.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 272, 'Cook or order your favorite meal after a hard repair conversation, as a small kindness to yourself.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 273, 'Talk to yourself the way you''d talk to a child who spilled juice after an honest mistake today.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 274, 'Try writing an apology with only one "sorry" in it, placed at the very beginning.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 275, 'When guilt shows up at night about an old mistake, write it down and tell yourself you''ll look at it in the morning.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 276, 'Ask a friend to point out, gently, when you apologize for no reason during your next hangout.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 277, 'Notice where the urge to over-apologize comes from, like a family habit, and write one line about it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 278, 'Say "Let me try that again" when you stumble over words, instead of apologizing for the stumble.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 279, 'When a mistake of yours is small and already fixed, say "Fixed it" rather than apologizing at all.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 280, 'Write an apology you once got that felt hollow, and list what was missing from it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 281, 'Decide on one phrase you''ll use when an apology is not owed, like "No problem" or "Good point," and use it today.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 282, 'Notice when you apologize for other people''s mistakes at work to keep the peace, and let them own it once.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 283, 'Give yourself a set time, like fifteen minutes, to feel bad about a mistake, then shift to a planned task.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 284, 'Accept an apology from someone you love by saying what you''d like going forward, simply and kindly.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 285, 'Admit to yourself one mistake you blamed on circumstance this month, and reclaim it in writing.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 286, 'Resist apologizing when you take up an armrest, a seat or a spot on a bench that is fairly yours.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 287, 'Tell yourself "I''ve already said sorry, now I''m showing it" when you feel the urge to apologize again.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 288, 'Read a favorite poem, quote or passage about forgiveness and copy one line into your notebook.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 289, 'Stop saying "I''m the worst" after mistakes, and try "That wasn''t my best, here''s my fix."'),
  ('apologizing-well', 290, 'When you feel defensive during feedback, say "Give me a second to take that in" and take the second.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 291, 'Notice whether your apology asks the other person to comfort you, and rewrite it so it doesn''t.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 292, 'Remind yourself before sleep that a repaired mistake is a finished chapter, and turn off the light.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 293, 'Look back over this challenge so far and pick the apology habit that has changed the most for you.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 294, 'Shovel a neighbor''s walk this winter if your snowplow or shovel pushed snow onto their side.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 295, 'Bring back a borrowed tool, lawn mower or ladder this spring, cleaned and with a thank you note attached.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 296, 'On a summer afternoon, invite someone you owe an apology to for a popsicle or iced tea on your porch.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 297, 'In the fall, rake a neighbor''s yard or share apples as a peace offering after a disagreement.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 298, 'Wake up early and write one apology before checking your phone, while your mind is clear.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 299, 'Make a list at breakfast of any loose ends from last week that might need a quick repair.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 300, 'At noon, pause and ask whether anything from your morning needs a brief acknowledgment.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 301, 'Use a slow drive home to decide whether a work tension needs an apology or just a conversation.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 302, 'Write a thank you card to someone who once gave you a good apology, telling them how it helped.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 303, 'Offer to pay for a friend''s dry cleaning, repair or replacement when you spill on them or their things.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 304, 'Send flowers or a small gift only after a clear verbal apology, never as a replacement for one.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 305, 'Fix a typo or error in something you shared with others and send a short correction note.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 306, 'Replace a library book, board game piece or kitchen tool you lost that belonged to someone else.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 307, 'Ask the person you hurt what "making it right" would look like, then do the doable part this week.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 308, 'Follow through on a changed behavior you promised in an apology, and quietly mark each time you do it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 309, 'Write a recipe card or share a family meal with someone as a warm follow-up after making amends.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 310, 'Pick up the tab for a friend''s coffee as part of repair, and use the time to listen more than you talk.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 311, 'When you break a dish at someone''s home, clean it up with them and send a replacement within the week.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 312, 'Notice one small repair you can make in your house today that you''ve been apologizing for putting off.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 313, 'Call a friend on the phone instead of texting, if your last apology to them felt too quick.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 314, 'Write an apology in the sand, on a steamy window or in the snow, just for yourself, then watch it disappear.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 315, 'Read aloud one apology you have been avoiding, as if to the person, while walking in a park.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 316, 'Mail a postcard from a trip to someone you''ve been meaning to reconnect with, owning the long quiet.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 317, 'Ask a friend how they''d like to receive apologies, such as in person, by text or with a gesture.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 318, 'Share with a friend or partner which phrase has helped you most in this challenge.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 319, 'Practice owning a mistake in a game night or sports match, like a missed pass, with a quick "My bad, I''ve got the next one."'),
  ('apologizing-well', 320, 'Tell a teammate in a pickup game or league that you''re sorry you argued a call, and shake hands.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 321, 'Apologize to a pet sitter, babysitter or house cleaner for unclear instructions, and write clearer ones.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 322, 'On a rainy day indoors, write down any unfinished apologies and choose the one to address this month.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 323, 'Set aside an old grudge you are carrying about an apology you never got, and write "I release this" beside it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 324, 'Tell an elder in your community you''re sorry you haven''t visited, and plan a visit for this week.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 325, 'Leave a warm online review for a business that fixed its mistake with you, naming what they did well.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 326, 'Say "Thank you for giving me another chance" to someone who kept trusting you after a slip.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 327, 'Give a coworker a heads-up before you change something that affects them, so an apology isn''t needed later.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 328, 'Say "I overreacted" plainly the next time you know you did, and ask how you can reset.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 329, 'Spend a quiet morning reviewing your promises for the week, and let go of any you can''t keep before you break them.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 330, 'When you realize you misremembered a shared story, correct yourself on the spot: "Actually, you''re right."'),
  ('apologizing-well', 331, 'Write an apology to your younger self for a hard choice you made, and thank them for surviving it.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 332, 'Try a two-sentence apology on a real situation: what you did and what you''ll do. Notice what the other person says.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 333, 'When a friend apologizes in a clumsy way, focus on their intent and thank them for trying.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 334, 'Plan a weekend repair project, like patching a fence or fixing a gate, that you once promised a neighbor.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 335, 'Come clean with your partner if you''ve been saying "I''m fine" when you weren''t, and share what''s really going on.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 336, 'Tell a friend "I''ve been thinking about what I said and I want to take it back" and then do.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 337, 'Talk to a coworker on a quiet Friday afternoon about a tension from earlier in the week, owning your part first.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 338, 'Listen for how people you admire apologize, and borrow one phrase from them that feels natural to you.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 339, 'Explain to a child why you''re writing a thank you or apology note, and let them add a drawing.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 340, 'Drop off a meal for a friend you haven''t supported during a hard season, with a note owning your absence.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 341, 'Tell a coworker you''re sorry you gossiped about them, and stop repeating the story to others.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 342, 'Pay back a small loan you forgot about, with a message that simply says "This is overdue, thank you."'),
  ('apologizing-well', 343, 'Keep an apology from sliding into a lecture, even if the other person also made mistakes.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 344, 'Pick one person you hurt years ago and write down one detail about them that makes you smile.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 345, 'Ask yourself on a Sunday evening whether any conversation from the week needs a follow-up or a repair.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 346, 'Say yes to the next invitation from a friend you once let down, and show up on time.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 347, 'When you catch yourself saying "I''m sorry you feel that way," stop and say what you actually did instead.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 348, 'Walk someone to their car or bus stop after an apology, keeping the talk easy and light.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 349, 'Write a short list of the ways you like to make amends, from fixing things to spending time together.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 350, 'Tell a stranger who helped you after your mistake, like a jumped car battery, how grateful you are.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 351, 'Offer a sincere apology to someone younger than you, a niece, a student or an intern, and treat it as seriously as any other.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 352, 'Notice a news story or public figure''s apology and decide what they owned and what they dodged.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 353, 'Say "Please forgive me" once this season to someone who matters, if the harm was truly yours.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 354, 'Wrap up a hard apology conversation by asking, "Is there anything else you need me to hear?"'),
  ('apologizing-well', 355, 'Return a phone call you''ve been avoiding because of guilt, and start with "I''ve been avoiding this call."'),
  ('apologizing-well', 356, 'Let a friend know you''ve been distant because of your own busy season, not anything they did, and that you miss them.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 357, 'Write a list of five apologies you''ve made during this challenge and circle the one that felt most honest.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 358, 'Tell a partner or friend you''re sorry you ruined a surprise or broke a confidence, and plan how to rebuild trust.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 359, 'Leave your pride at the door when you visit someone to repair things, by arriving with a question instead of a speech.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 360, 'Show up early to the next gathering after an apology and help set up, as a quiet sign of goodwill.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 361, 'Write your own short guide to apologizing well in three lines, and tape it inside a kitchen cabinet.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 362, 'Choose one reflexive "sorry" you''ve already replaced and notice how natural the new phrase feels now.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 363, 'Thank someone who taught you, by example, how to own mistakes, and tell them one moment you remember.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 364, 'Name one relationship that feels steadier since you began this challenge, and do one kind thing for that person.'),
  ('apologizing-well', 365, 'Close out the week by writing one mistake, one repair, and one thing you''ll carry forward.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 1, 'Write down the names of five people you love who live far away, then pick one to contact today.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 2, 'Send a short text to a faraway friend that simply says you thought of them this morning.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 3, 'Record a thirty second voice note telling a relative about the best part of your day.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 4, 'Snap a photo of your breakfast and send it to someone who used to share meals with you.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 5, 'Look up the time where your far-off family lives and note the best hour to reach them.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 6, 'Set a recurring reminder to call one distant relative at the same time each week.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 7, 'Buy a small stack of postcards to keep by the door for quick notes to faraway people.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 8, 'Write a postcard to an old friend and mention one memory you both share.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 9, 'Ask a sibling who lives far away what they are cooking for dinner tonight.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 10, 'Put every faraway birthday you know into your calendar with a reminder three days ahead.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 11, 'Text an old school friend a photo of something that reminded you of them.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 12, 'Call a grandparent and ask them what the weather is like where they are.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 13, 'Start a shared photo album with a faraway relative and add three pictures from this week.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 14, 'Tell someone far away, in plain words, that you miss them.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 15, 'Send a voice note from your walk so a faraway friend can hear the birds or the traffic.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 16, 'Mail a handwritten letter to a relative who does not use the internet much.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 17, 'Plan a video chat for this weekend and send the invite now so it is on both calendars.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 18, 'Pick a book that you and a distant friend can both read, then agree on a first chapter.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 19, 'Ask your mom or dad for one family recipe you have never made yourself.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 20, 'Share a song that fits your mood today with someone who lives in another state.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 21, 'Write three questions you would like to ask a faraway grandparent and keep them for your next call.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 22, 'Reply to a message from a faraway friend that you have been meaning to answer.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 23, 'Send a photo of your street at dusk to someone who has never seen where you live.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 24, 'Find out one small thing happening in a distant relative''s week, like a dentist visit, and ask about it later.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 25, 'Call an old coworker you liked and ask how the new job or retirement is going.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 26, 'Choose a movie a faraway friend loves and watch it tonight, then text them one favorite scene.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 27, 'Tuck a note in with a bill payment reminder so you remember to write to a relative this month.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 28, 'Send a quick good morning text timed to arrive as a faraway friend wakes up.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 29, 'Ask a sibling about a childhood memory and see whether you remember it the same way.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 30, 'Put together a small care package with a snack from your town and a note.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 31, 'Text a faraway cousin to ask what they are looking forward to this season.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 32, 'Tell a distant friend about something small that went wrong today and how you handled it.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 33, 'Draw a quick doodle, photograph it, and send it to a niece or nephew who lives far away.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 34, 'Look through old photos and send one to the person in it with a line about that day.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 35, 'Make a list of faraway people you have not heard from in over a year.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 36, 'Send a brief message to one person on your quiet list, with no pressure to reply quickly.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 37, 'Call a relative during your commute or while folding laundry so the chat fits your day.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 38, 'Ask a far-off friend to send you a photo of their view right now, and send yours back.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 39, 'Ask a faraway friend which hour of their day is calmest for a phone call.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 40, 'Mail a newspaper clipping or local flyer that a faraway relative would find funny.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 41, 'Ask a grandparent to tell you how they met their best friend.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 42, 'Set up a standing monthly call with a sibling and give it a name you both like.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 43, 'Send a text that starts with "This made me think of you" and a photo or link.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 44, 'Tell a faraway friend about a small win this week and ask about one of theirs.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 45, 'Write a thank you note to a distant relative for something they did years ago.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 46, 'Record a short video of your pet doing something silly and send it to family far away.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 47, 'Ask your faraway parent what they had for lunch and tell them what you had.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 48, 'Plan a time to watch the same game or show as a relative and text during it.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 49, 'Send a birthday card early this time so it arrives before the day, not after.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 50, 'Call an old friend from a past job and share one inside joke you still remember.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 51, 'Ask someone far away how they are really doing, and wait for the full answer.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 52, 'Let a faraway friend know when you are having a rough day instead of saying everything is fine.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 53, 'Choose one faraway person to send a small, silly thing to every week this season.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 54, 'Photograph your grocery cart or your farmers market haul and send it to a relative who loves to cook.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 55, 'Invite a faraway relative to cook the same recipe as you over video tonight or this weekend.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 56, 'Save a family recipe card by photographing it and sending a copy to your siblings.'),
  ('keeping-in-touch-from-a-distance', 57, 'Ask a distant friend what book, show or podcast they are into and try a little of it.'),
